---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Hero from "@/components/Hero.astro";
import Grid from "@/ui/Grid.astro";
import Heading from "@/ui/Heading.astro";
import "@/styles/legal.css";
import { getPortfolioData } from "@/lib/portfolio-cache";

export const prerender = false;

const { profile, contact } = await getPortfolioData();
const fullName = [profile?.first_name, profile?.last_name]
    .filter(Boolean)
    .join(" ");
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy">
    <Hero
        staticText="Privacy Policy"
        dynamicText={false}
        compact={true}
        tagSize="h1"
    />
    <Grid cols={1} rows={1}>
        <div class="box bg-solid legal-content">
            <Heading tagName="h2" tagSize="h2" animated={true}>
                1. An overview of data protection
            </Heading>

            <Heading tagName="h3" tagSize="h3">
                General information
            </Heading>
            <p>
                This section gives you a quick overview of what happens to your personal data when you visit my
                portfolio website. “Personal data” means information that can identify you, either directly or when
                combined with other information. You’ll find more details about how I handle that information and how
                you can contact me in the sections below.
            </p>

            <Heading tagName="h3" tagSize="h3">
                Data recording on this website
            </Heading>

            <Heading tagName="h4" tagSize="h4">
                Who is the responsible party for the recording of data on this website (i.e., the “controller”)?
            </Heading>
            <p>
                I’m responsible for handling personal data collected through this website. In data protection law, this
                is called being the “controller.” You can find my contact details in the section “Who is responsible
                for this website?”
            </p>

            <Heading tagName="h4" tagSize="h4">
                How do I record your data?
            </Heading>
            <p>
                I receive personal data when you choose to share it with me. This may, for instance be
                information you enter by submitting a recommendation about me or filling other forms.<br><br>

                Some technical information, such as your browser, operating system, or the time you visit the site, may
                also be recorded automatically by the systems that run this website. This happens when you access the
                site.
            </p>

            <Heading tagName="h4" tagSize="h4">
                What are the purposes I use your data for?
            </Heading>
            <p>
                I use technical information to keep my portfolio website running properly and to troubleshoot problems.
                If you submit a recommendation about me, I use the information you provide to review it and, where
                appropriate, include it in my portfolio.
            </p>

            <Heading tagName="h4" tagSize="h4">
                What rights do you have over your personal data?
            </Heading>
            <p>
                You have the right to ask me what personal data I hold about you, where it came from, whether it has
                been shared and with whom, and why I use it. You can also ask me to correct inaccurate information or,
                in certain circumstances, delete it or restrict how I use it.<br><br>

                If I rely on your consent to use your data, you can withdraw that consent at any time. This won’t
                affect any use of your data that took place before you withdrew it. Depending on the circumstances, you
                may also have the right to object to certain uses of your data or ask for a copy of it in a portable
                format.<br><br>

                You can also lodge a complaint with your local data protection supervisory authority. If you have a
                question or want to exercise one of these rights, please contact me using the details in this policy.
            </p>


            <Heading tagName="h2" tagSize="h2" animated={true}>
                2. External Hosting of my website
            </Heading>
            <p>
                I host this website with netcup GmbH. To make the website available and keep it secure, the hosting
                provider may process technical information about visits, such as IP addresses, the pages requested,
                access times, browser details, and error logs. If you submit a recommendation through a form on this
                website, the information you enter may also be processed by the hosting provider.<br><br>

                I use this hosting service to make my portfolio available online and to ensure that it runs reliably
                and securely. Where applicable, this processing is based on my legitimate interests under Art. 6(1)(f)
                GDPR. In plain terms, this means I have a legitimate need to operate and protect my website, while
                respecting your privacy.<br><br>

                My hosting provider processes personal data only as needed to provide the hosting service and in
                accordance with my instructions.<br><br>

                Hosting provider:<br><br>

                netcup GmbH<br>
                Emmy-Noether-Straße 10<br>
                D-76131 Karlsruhe
            </p>

            <Heading tagName="h4" tagSize="h4">
                My agreement with the hosting provider
            </Heading>
            <p>
                I have a data processing agreement (DPA) with netcup for hosting this website. A DPA is a contract
                required by data protection law. It sets out that netcup processes personal data on my behalf, follows
                my documented instructions, and handles the data in line with the GDPR.
            </p>

            <Heading tagName="h3" tagSize="h3">
                Website security and delivery (Cloudflare)
            </Heading>
            <p>
                I use Cloudflare, Inc., 101 Townsend St., San Francisco, CA 94107, USA (after referred to as
                “Cloudflare”), to provide DNS and content delivery services and to help protect my portfolio website.
                <br><br>

                My website is proxied through Cloudflare, so requests from your browser pass through Cloudflare’s
                network before reaching my server. Cloudflare may process technical information such as your IP address,
                browser and device details, the pages or files you request, and information about network traffic. This
                allows Cloudflare to deliver website content and act as a filter between your browser and my server,
                helping to identify and block malicious or unwanted traffic.<br><br>

                Depending on the security features in use, Cloudflare may also use cookies or similar technologies to
                help distinguish legitimate visitors from automated or potentially harmful traffic.<br><br>

                I use Cloudflare to help keep my website available, reliable, and secure. This is based on my
                legitimate interest under Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. In simple terms, I have a legitimate reason to operate and
                protect my website while respecting your privacy.<br><br>

                Data transmission to the US is based on the Standard Contractual Clauses (SCC) of the European
                Commission. Details and further information on security and data protection at Cloudflare can be found
                here:<br>
                <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                    https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/
                </a>.<br><br>

                The company is certified in accordance with the “EU-US Data Privacy Framework” (DPF). The DPF is an
                agreement between the European Union and the US, which is intended to ensure compliance with European
                data protection standards for data processing in the US. Every company certified under the DPF is
                obliged to comply with these data protection standards. For more information, please contact the
                provider under the following link:<br>
                <a href="https://www.dataprivacyframework.gov/participant/5666" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                    https://www.dataprivacyframework.gov/participant/5666
                </a>.
            </p>


            <Heading tagName="h2" tagSize="h2" animated={true}>
                3. General information and mandatory information
            </Heading>
            <Heading tagName="h3" tagSize="h3">
                How I handle and protect your personal data
            </Heading>
            <p>
                I take the privacy of visitors to my portfolio website seriously. I handle personal data in line with
                applicable data protection laws and the information in this policy.<br><br>

                When you visit my website, some technical information may be processed so the site can be delivered and
                kept secure. If you choose to send me information — for example, by submitting a recommendation about me
                for my portfolio — I use it as described in this policy.<br><br>

                Please keep in mind that sending information over the internet, including by email, can involve
                security risks. Although I take reasonable steps to protect personal data, no method of transmission or
                storage can be guaranteed to be completely secure.
            </p>

            <Heading tagName="h3" tagSize="h3">
                Who is responsible for this website?
            </Heading>
            <div class="legal-section">
                <p>
                    I’m the person responsible for handling personal data on this website. In data protection law, this
                    role is called the “controller.”<br>
                </p>

                <p>Contact details:<br></p>

                <div class="contact-block">
                    <p>{fullName}</p>
                    <address>{contact.address}</address>
                </div>

                <p>
                    Phone: <a href={`tel:${contact.phone}`}>{contact.phone}</a><br/>
                    E-mail: <a href={`mailto:${contact.mail}`}>{contact.mail}</a>
                </p>

                <p>
                    The controller is the person or organisation that decides why and how personal data is processed
                    (for example, names or email addresses). In this case, that’s me.<br/><br/>

                    I may not always be able to answer the phone right away. If your number is visible, I’ll do
                    my best to call you back. If you’ve withheld your caller ID, I won’t be able to return your call.
                </p>
            </div>

            <Heading tagName="h3" tagSize="h3">
                How long I keep your information
            </Heading>
            <p>
                I keep personal data only for as long as it is needed for the purpose it was collected for, unless this
                policy explains a different retention period.<br><br>

                I keep recommendations for my portfolio while they remain relevant and reasonably up to date. If a
                recommendation is replaced, becomes outdated, or I have reason to believe it no longer reflects the
                person’s views or our professional/personal relationship, I’ll remove it or stop displaying it. If I
                can no longer stay in contact with the person who provided it and can’t reasonably confirm that it is
                still valid, I may also remove it.<br><br>

                I may need to keep some information for longer where the law requires it
                or permits it, for example to meet legal record-keeping obligations.
            </p>

            <Heading tagName="h3" tagSize="h3">
                Why I’m allowed to use personal data (legal basis)
            </Heading>
            <p>
                The legal basis for using personal data depends on what I’m using it for. For example, when someone
                submits a recommendation and agrees that I may display it in my portfolio, I may rely on their consent
                under Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR. They can withdraw that consent at any time; I’ll then stop displaying or
                delete the recommendation.<br><br>

                I may rely on my legitimate interests under Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR to operate, maintain, and protect my
                website (for example, when processing technical information needed to keep it secure). This means I
                have a legitimate reason for that processing, while still taking your rights and privacy into account.
                <br><br>

                In some cases, I may need to process personal data to meet a legal obligation under Art. 6(1)(c) GDPR.
                If a different legal basis applies to a particular use of your data, I’ll explain it in the relevant
                section of this policy.<br><br>
            </p>

            <Heading tagName="h3" tagSize="h3">
                Who may process your personal data?
            </Heading>
            <p>
                I use netcup to host my portfolio website and Cloudflare to help deliver and protect it. When you visit
                the website, these providers may process technical information such as your IP address and details of
                your request as needed to provide their services.<br><br>

                I have a data processing agreement with netcup. Any personal data processed by netcup on my behalf is
                handled under that agreement and in line with my instructions. Cloudflare processes information as part
                of the services it provides for my website; you can find more details about this in the Cloudflare
                section of this policy.<br><br>

                I don’t share personal data with any other organisations for any marketing purposes. I only disclose
                it if I’m legally required to do so.<br><br>
            </p>

            <Heading tagName="h3" tagSize="h3">
                Withdrawing your consent
            </Heading>
            <p>
                If I use your personal data based on your consent, you can withdraw that consent at any time by
                contacting me. For example, if you withdraw your consent to have a recommendation displayed in my
                portfolio, I’ll remove it from the website. Withdrawing your consent won’t undo what I did with your
                personal data while you had given permission for me to use it. Once you withdraw your consent, I’ll
                stop displaying it in my portfolio. I’ll also delete the information if I no longer need to keep it for
                another lawful reason.
            </p>

            <Heading tagName="h3" tagSize="h3">
                Your right to object to certain uses of your data (Art. 21 GDPR)
            </Heading>

            <p>
                IF I PROCESS YOUR PERSONAL DATA BASED ON MY LEGITIMATE INTERESTS UNDER ART. 6(1)(F) GDPR, YOU CAN
                OBJECT AT ANY TIME FOR REASONS RELATED TO YOUR PARTICULAR SITUATION. I WILL THEN STOP PROCESSING YOUR
                DATA UNLESS I CAN SHOW COMPELLING LEGITIMATE GROUNDS THAT OVERRIDE YOUR INTERESTS, RIGHTS AND FREEDOMS,
                OR I NEED THE DATA TO ESTABLISH, EXERCISE OR DEFEND LEGAL CLAIMS.<br><br>

                IF YOU HAVE A QUESTION OR WANT TO OBJECT, PLEASE CONTACT ME USING THE CONTACT DETAILS IN THIS POLICY.
            </p>

            <Heading tagName="h3" tagSize="h3">
                Your right to contact a data protection authority
            </Heading>
            <p>
                If you believe that I have handled your personal data in a way that violates data protection law, you
                have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority. You can usually
                contact the authority where you live or work, or where you believe the issue took place. You can do
                this even if you also choose to pursue other legal remedies.
            </p>

            <Heading tagName="h3" tagSize="h3">
                Your right to receive or transfer your data
            </Heading>
            <p>
                Where the right to data portability applies, you can ask me to provide personal data you have given me
                in a commonly used, machine-readable format. This right applies when I process the data automatically
                based on your consent or a contract with you. Where technically feasible, you can also ask me to send
                the data directly to another controller.
            </p>

            <Heading tagName="h3" tagSize="h3">
                Your right to access, correct, or delete your data
            </Heading>
            <p>
                You can ask me whether I hold personal data about you and, where the law gives you this right, request
                a copy. You can also ask where the data came from, who it has been shared with, and why I use it. If
                any information is inaccurate, you can ask me to correct it. In certain circumstances, you can also ask
                me to delete it. If you have a question or would like to make a request, please contact me using the
                details in this policy.
            </p>

            <Heading tagName="h3" tagSize="h3">
                Your right to restrict how I use your data
            </Heading>
            <p>
                In certain situations, you can ask me to temporarily restrict the processing of your personal data.
                This right may apply:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    If you believe your personal data is inaccurate, while I check it.
                </li>
                <li>
                    If you believe I have processed your data unlawfully and you would prefer me to restrict its use
                    rather than delete it.
                </li>
                <li>
                    If I no longer need your data, but you need it to establish, exercise, or defend a legal claim.
                </li>
                <li>
                    If you have objected to my processing under Art. 21(1) GDPR, while I assess whether my interests or
                    your rights and interests take priority.
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                When processing is restricted, I will generally store your data but not otherwise use it. The law
                allows certain exceptions, such as where you consent, where the data is needed for a legal claim, or
                where processing is necessary to protect another person’s rights or for an important public interest.
                If you’d like to request a restriction, please contact me using the details in this policy.
            </p>

            <Heading tagName="h3" tagSize="h3">
                SSL and/or TLS encryption (HTTPS)
            </Heading>
            <p>
                This website uses HTTPS to help protect information sent between your browser and the website. You can
                usually tell the connection is encrypted when the address starts with “https://” and your browser shows
                a lock icon.<br><br>

                Encryption helps prevent others from reading information while it is being transmitted, for example
                when you submit a recommendation. It does not guarantee complete security or protect information once
                it reaches the website or the service providers that process it.
            </p>


            <Heading tagName="h2" tagSize="h2" animated={true}>
                4. Recording of data on this website
            </Heading>
            <Heading tagName="h3" tagSize="h3">
                Contacting me by email or phone
            </Heading>
            <p>
                If you contact me by email or phone, I’ll use the information you provide (such as your name, contact
                details, and message) to respond to you. If you call and your number is visible, I may use it to call
                you back if I’m unable to answer.<br><br>

                I process this information to handle your request. This is generally based on my legitimate interest in
                responding to enquiries (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). I keep the information only for as long as needed to deal
                with your enquiry, unless I’m required by law to keep it for longer. I don’t share it with others
                unless this is necessary to handle your request or I’m legally required to do so.
            </p>


            <Heading tagName="h2" tagSize="h2" animated={true}>
                5. Plug-ins and Tools
            </Heading>
            <Heading tagName="h3" tagSize="h3">
                Google Fonts (local embedding)
            </Heading>
            <p>
                My website uses so-called Google Fonts provided by Google to ensure the uniform use of fonts on this
                site. These Google fonts are locally installed so that a connection to Google’s servers will not be
                established in conjunction with this application.<br><br>

                For more information on Google Fonts, please follow this link:<br>
                <a href="https://developers.google.com/fonts/faq" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                    https://developers.google.com/fonts/faq
                </a><br><br>

                and consult Google’s Data Privacy Declaration under:<br>
                <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy?hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                    https://policies.google.com/privacy?hl=en
                </a><br><br>
            </p>
        </div>
    </Grid>
</Layout>